figdown 0.1 block
# spec §12.3: absent is OMITTED, and an explicitly EMPTY label is a
# WRITTEN value — a third state, recorded uniformly on all nine
# label-bearing directives and on `title` (`EMPTY-LABEL-STATE`, 0.1;
# DISCREPANCIES `EMPTY-LABEL-DIRECTIVE-COVERAGE` resolved). The companion fixture
# 214-label-absent-vs-id freezes the absent half: read the two goldens
# together and the rule is the contrast between them. The id
# substitution is a RENDERING rule that applies only to absence, so
# every label written below draws nothing at all.
title ""
plane over ""
node a ""
group g ""
external x ""
node b "" in=g
edge a -> b
bundle bl "" a--b
bitfield hdr "" numbering=lsb0
field "ver" 4
table t ""
| A |
|---|
| 1 |
timing w ""
signal clk 0101
